{
 "thread": "hHdXekFlPeo",
 "subject": "How to estimate individual encounter probabilities when sigma estimates for both mixture classes differ?",
 "messages_listed": 6,
 "last_activity": "2020-01-14T20:02:58Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "4rOaEiQhCwAJ",
   "from": "IntoTheBlue574",
   "author": "c0f1ca3e47b2822d",
   "date": "2020-01-13T18:36:33Z",
   "subject": "How to estimate individual encounter probabilities when sigma estimates for both mixture classes differ?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"verdana, sans-serif\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\" color=\"#000000\">Hello everyone, </font><div><font face=\"verdana, sans-serif\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\" color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"verdana, sans-serif\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\" color=\"#000000\">I am working on a <span style=\"font-size:12px\">my master&#39;s project using a spatially explicit capture-recapture approach to model the exposure of whale watching boats on sperm whales in the Central Azores. </span></font></div><div><font face=\"verdana, sans-serif\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\" color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I am analyzing my capture-recapture data using the R &#39;secr&#39; package to develop different models accounting for sampling effort and heterogeneity in sigma or/and g0 (a detailed list of the models used and outputs is attached below). </span></font><span style=\"font-size:12px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">The model parameters are used for estimating encounter probabilities for each individual in each 1x1km2 grid cell. My results indicate that the best fitting model for my data is based on a half-normal detection function, accounting for heterogeneity in sigma. </span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">As the output of the secr model fit includes two different estimates for sigma for both mixture classes, I am not sure, which of this estimates to use for calculating the individual encounter probabilities. In comparison, the values for the lambda0 estimates are equal in both mixture classes, so I don&#39;t have to choose.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">What is the difference between the two estimated parameters? How do I decide which of them to use? </span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">As they yield quite different results in the further probability estimates, it would be important for me to understand how this model estimates the parameters and how to interpret the model output.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">I am greatly appreciating any help on this topic! </span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Chiara</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Example of the modeling process</span></div><div><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">model.used&lt;-secr.fit(secr.obj,model=list(g0~1,sigma~h2),mask=hab.mask,detectfn=0,trace=F)</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><div style=\"padding-left:1em;margin-top:1em;margin-bottom:1em;border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid;min-height:12px;color:rgb(102,0,102);border-color:rgb(102,0,102);background-color:rgb(238,238,238);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">predict(model.used)<br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px\"></div><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">$`session = 1, h2 = 1`</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">       link     estimate  SE.estimate          lcl          ucl</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">D       log 1.155845e-03 6.010725e-04 4.430554e-04 3.015373e-03</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">g0    logit <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,242,204)\">6.702131e-02</span> 2.025034e-02 3.668150e-02 1.193466e-01</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">sigma   log <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,217,102)\">1.227834e+04</span> 2.172605e+03 8.703262e+03 1.732196e+04</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">pmix  logit 5.357822e-02 4.429945e-02 1.011249e-02 2.387997e-01</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">$`session = 1, h2 = 2`</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">       link     estimate  SE.estimate          lcl          ucl</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">D       log 1.155845e-03 6.010725e-04 4.430554e-04 3.015373e-03</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">g0    logit <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,242,204)\">6.702131e-02</span> 2.025034e-02 3.668150e-02 1.193466e-01</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">sigma   log <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,217,102)\">2.563491e+03</span> 8.098543e+02 1.400525e+03 4.692157e+03</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">pmix  logit 9.464218e-01 4.429945e-02 7.612003e-01 9.898875e-01</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">#Estimating individual encounter probabilities for each 1x1km2 grid cell of the habitat mask</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">number.animals&lt;-attributes(secr.obj)$dim[1]</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://pr.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pr.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487274553000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ONDEuj2Fq61Ahy4uiwcVo\">pr.int</a>&lt;-array(0,c(length(hab.mask[,1]),number.animals)) #Creates a matrix of zeros, with the same number of rows as grid cells in the habitat mask (j) and the same number of columns as marked individuals (i)</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">for(i in 1:number.animals){                                     #A loop for every individual that was marked</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">  pdf&lt;-fxi.secr(model.used,i=i,X=hab.mask)                        #Estimates the probability density function of the home range centers for individual i for every cell in the habitat mask</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">  pr&lt;-array(0,c(length(hab.mask[,1]),length(hab.mask[,1])))       #Storage matrix for encounter probabilities. Creates a matrix of zeros, with the same number of rows and columns as the number of cells in the habitat mask</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">  for(j in 1:length(hab.mask[,1])){                           #Runs a loop for every cell in the habitat mask</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">    #Estimates the probability of encountering individual i for every grid cell in the habitat mask, when the home range center of individual i is located in grid cell j. The probability is estimated over 1 SO (i.e. 1 second)</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">    enc.prob&lt;-1-exp(-<span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,242,204)\">lamda</span>*exp((-(sqrt(abs(hab.mask$x[j]-hab.mask$x)^2+abs(hab.mask$y[j]-hab.mask$y)^2)^2))/(2*<span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,217,102)\">sigma</span>^2))) #Half normal detection function</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">    pr[,j]&lt;-enc.prob*pdf[j]     #Multiplies the estimated encounter probabilities with the probability density function of cell j in the habitat mask (part of the spatial integration)</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">  }</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">  <a href=\"http://pr.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pr.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487274553000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ONDEuj2Fq61Ahy4uiwcVo\">pr.int</a>[,i]&lt;-rowSums(pr)         #Adds the sum for each cell in the habitat mask for individual i (integrates the results over all cells in the habitat mask for individual i)</span><br style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">}</span><span style=\"font-size:12px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><br></span></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "6u5-haQ0CwAJ",
   "from": "Murray Efford",
   "author": "118cea91a1619106",
   "date": "2020-01-14T00:33:55Z",
   "subject": "Re: How to estimate individual encounter probabilities when sigma estimates for both mixture classes differ?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The heterogeneity model is a 2-class finite mixture model, meaning that variation in the detection parameter is modelled as if it resulted from 2 distinct classes of individual. The estimates relate to the 2 classes; note also the mixing parameter pmix. I suppose you want the weighted average of the two (weighted by pmix). See also <a href=\"https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-finitemixtures.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-finitemixtures.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487274554000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0s3ni0tV7bfD5fmIoPW6j2\">https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-finitemixtures.pdf</a></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "O0NQ3pVVCwAJ",
   "from": "IntoTheBlue574",
   "author": "c0f1ca3e47b2822d",
   "date": "2020-01-14T10:37:36Z",
   "subject": "Re: How to estimate individual encounter probabilities when sigma estimates for both mixture classes differ?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">So in this example would the weighted mean be calculated like this?<div><br></div><div>(<span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">1.227834e+04 * </span><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">5.357822e-02 + </span><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">2.563491e+03 * </span><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">9.464218e-01) / 2 = 1.541998</span><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">e+03</span><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"> </span></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>Am Montag, 13. Januar 2020 23:33:55 UTC-1 schrieb Murray Efford:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The heterogeneity model is a 2-class finite mixture model, meaning that variation in the detection parameter is modelled as if it resulted from 2 distinct classes of individual. The estimates relate to the 2 classes; note also the mixing parameter pmix. I suppose you want the weighted average of the two (weighted by pmix). See also <a href=\"https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-finitemixtures.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-finitemixtures.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487274556000&amp;usg=AOvVaw08hAQZNPjxep247Wfy2GVk\">https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-finitemixtures.pdf</a></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "zvx81vBwCwAJ",
   "from": "Murray Efford",
   "author": "118cea91a1619106",
   "date": "2020-01-14T18:58:54Z",
   "subject": "Re: How to estimate individual encounter probabilities when sigma estimates for both mixture classes differ?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>It&#39;s a mistake to divide by 2. Otherwise, yes.<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div>On Tuesday, January 14, 2020 at 11:37:36 PM UTC+13, IntoTheBlue574 wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">So in this example would the weighted mean be calculated like this?<div><br></div><div>(<span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">1.227834e+04 * </span><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">5.357822e-02 + </span><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">2.563491e+03 * </span><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">9.464218e-01) / 2 = 1.541998</span><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\">e+03</span><span style=\"color:rgb(78,78,78);font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12px\"> </span><br><br>Am Montag, 13. Januar 2020 23:33:55 UTC-1 schrieb Murray Efford:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The heterogeneity model is a 2-class finite mixture model, meaning that variation in the detection parameter is modelled as if it resulted from 2 distinct classes of individual. The estimates relate to the 2 classes; note also the mixing parameter pmix. I suppose you want the weighted average of the two (weighted by pmix). See also <a href=\"https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-finitemixtures.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-finitemixtures.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487274558000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1wBoEIEDx-JJO3Z5fVy5CR\">https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-finitemixtures.pdf</a></div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
