sulted from 2 distinct classes of individual. The estimates relate to the 2 classes; note also the mixing parameter pmix. I suppose you want the weighted average of the two (weighted by pmix). See also <a href=\"https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-finitemixtures.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-finitemixtures.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487274560000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1-Fctimj-mrqzqZ1h2-9kQ\">https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-finitemixtures.pdf</a></div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>"
